nd turned her head slightly to look at the surrounding situation. The first thing she saw was the boat pole. Looking a little further away, she saw a crowd of people. Fragmented sounds penetrated her eardrums, which surprised her. Her clothes? He looked around hurriedly. This glance was enough to make her stunned. In just a few seconds, she realized what was happening. She touched the board with her little hands, grabbed her clothes, and tried to cover herself up. The hatred and humiliation in her heart made her bite her lower lip. He grabbed his clothes with both hands and clenched them into fists, tightly, tightly. She reluctantly sat up with her fingers supporting the ship's board. The torn clothes covered important parts. The scars on her body were reflected in her eyes, and she could not see any joy or anger. When things had reached this point, she had nothing to be afraid of, let alone anything to care about. \"Well...\" I wanted to stand up, but I didn't expect to pull the scar on my chest, and the tearing pain suddenly hit me again. Suppressing the pain, Lanya noticed her current location, the ship. She was on a classic and luxurious ship. The scenery in the distance was classical. Before she could fully appreciate it, a sudden coldness hit her back. She felt a cold gaze staring at her, like a wild wolf locking its prey in the middle of the night, making her tremble all over. Turning his head alertly, he met a pair of cheetah-like eyes, which were cold and full of ridicule. Ridicule? Who is this man? Lanya looked at the person in front of her. He was dressed in ancient clothes and had long hair hanging down behind him. He was lying on a soft couch, exuding an awe-inspiring and cold aura. Such a man, such appearance and demeanor are intimidating. She, Lanya, had not met many men. In the past thirteen years, she had met less than a hundred men, but she knew it quite well through TV and books, but the sight of the man in front of her made her feel fear from the bottom of her heart. Her nails dug into her flesh, and a kind of fear filled her heart. She was obviously extremely frightened, but she raised her chin unwilling to admit defeat. \"Who are you?\" The hoarse voice was cold. She never knew when such a dangerous person came to the Silver Moon family. Zhuye Kuangming stood up from the soft couch, his slender legs lazily approached her, and his sexy lips gently highlighted a few words, which made Lan Ya tremble. \"The person who wants to kill you.\" Lanya stood up straight and took a deep breath, but she still couldn't figure out the current situation. The ancient costumes around her confused her. She could feel that this man was not from the Silver Moon family. If it's not the Silver Moon family, then who else wants to kill her? \"Who are you?\" Lan Ya emphasized, her thin body crumbling. Zhuye Kuangming moved his white fingers and lifted Lan Ya's chin. There was a mocking smile on his lips, but a murderous look in his eyes: \"The dead don't deserve to know.\"", "title_en": "Chapter 5"}